# ---- 1.02 Gameplay, fixes 9 and 13 (src/game/enhance/fixes102.h) in the levels' own hero_input_update / hero_set_state /
# hero_surface_update: the 1.02 build's changes to those functions (each level's copy changed as Veldin's), at the instruction of
# the level's code that corresponds to Veldin's point (the alignment of the two instruction streams; the 1.02 build's own copies
# read for each level). Veldin's points (the hand ports: hero_transitions.cpp, hero_state.cpp, hero_update.cpp):
#   P9a 0x22c0c8  hero_input_update, state 0x3f (the hoverboard's ready stance): gameplay102_board_ride_off: 2 at the common
#                 hero_set_state(a0, 1) of 0x231c10, else on to 0x22c118 (s0 the player block on both, as it is here)
#   P9c 0x231650  state 0x53: on deadly ground 0x58 (gameplay102_deadly_ground), at 0x231c10
#   P9d 0x23173c  state 0x59: 0x58 within 0.3 of deadly ground
#   P9e 0x231894  state 0x54: +0xa90 from the speed (the case's first store), then 0x58 within 0.2 of deadly ground
#   P9f 0x226f54  hero_set_state, state 0x53: on deadly ground, on the ground: 0x58 (gameplay102_deadly_landing(0)), return 0
#                 at the epilogue (0x2275fc, the target of the redirects' `b`)
#   P9g 0x227074  state 0x54: the same with the sub-state 1
#   P13 0x2225d8  hero_set_state, after hero_mode3_exit: the entered state stored again (gameplay102_mode3_left; a0_in the
#                 state, the function's first argument)
#   P9i 0x20be9c  hero_surface_update, quicksand: in a vehicle mode hero_lost, to the epilogue 0x20beb4 (Rilgar, Quartu and
#                 Veldin's finale only: the other copies have no quicksand and the 1.02 build left them as they were)
# With the fixes off each statement is a test that fails.

