# ---- The space fights' HUD (issue #82): with Options > Display > HUD wider than 4:3 in a widened view, the radar (the frame's right:
# its two background sprites at x 368, its blips about x 432) and the missiles (the frame's left: x 24..) of the player's ship's
# draw-list callback (Pokitaru L11:0x311d50, Gemlik Base L13:0x2b97f8 - Qwark's fight -, Drek's fleet L17:0x2eb9a8) move toward the
# edges as the HUD's side elements do: each call that draws one has its chain range noted (src/game/render/render_view.h
# render_view_hud_begin before the call, render_view_hud_end at its return address). Host bookkeeping only: the packet cursor read,
# nothing of the game's written; with the HUD at 4:3 (the default) begin notes nothing.
# The PAL builds keep these callers as NTSC-U has them (their addresses inside the region tables' code runs, data/regions/;
# checked on SCES-50916 1.00): no `PAL:` lines.
